lionclip (0.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Popup opening no longer costs more as the history grows: result rows are
    built in chunks and extended on scroll, instead of building and measuring
    every stored item on each open. Measured on Zorin GNOME/X11 with a full
    500-item history, 504 ms became 41 ms. Search, pin and delete rebuild the
    list too, and gain the same reduction.
  * Auto-paste no longer freezes the screen after choosing an item. Key
    synthesis moved from the XTEST extension to core SendEvent, so the
    compositor and its shell extensions no longer process each synthesized
    key. Note that a client which ignores events flagged as synthetic no
    longer receives the paste; the chosen item is still placed on the
    clipboard, so a manual Ctrl+V always works.
  * Restoring an item no longer reads its own payload back out of the X
    selection to identify it, which for an image meant decoding and re-hashing
    up to 25 MiB on a latency-sensitive path.

 -- Leonardo Vulczak <leonardovulczak@gmail.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

lionclip (0.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Desktop integration: final application ID, desktop entry, icon, autostart
    entry and the show/hide/toggle command surface.
  * First Debian package for Ubuntu 24.04 and Zorin OS based on noble.

 -- Leonardo Vulczak <leonardovulczak@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
